{
  "title": "confidence ranges: quantiles, order-statistic intervals and bounds, a heavy tail read robustly, timing floors kept apart, and duration forecasts, the same on every device",
  "covers": [
    "eleven task/high/feature samples: eight at 18 to 25 minutes over 2h and three at 20 minutes over a 5-minute estimate; the lower quantiles p10 p25 p50 p75 p90 read indices 1 2 5 7 9",
    "the median's order-statistic interval is ranks 3 to 9, 1914/2048; the bounds for one more sample are the range, 10/12, below 90% and said so, and the p10/p90 intervals miss 90% too",
    "the three 5-minute tickets sit 14.7 robust deviations above the standard median of ln(ratio): heavy_tail, and the expected ratio is the pooled ratio clipped at the fence (0.1825) instead of pooled (0.2379)",
    "two timing-floor records in that class are listed apart and never samples: floors_excluded",
    "a bug/low key with one sample and four floors reads its own key, floor_dominated, and an open bug/low forecasts the floor with a 60-second floor_bound expected figure, with or without an estimate",
    "an unstarted task/high/feature estimated at 4h has no model to match: its walk starts without the model, and it forecasts estimate times the ratio's quantiles, bounds and clipped expected ratio; one with no estimate reads no_estimate",
    "every figure is from replicated data, so the writer, the tail device and a hydrated device read the same ranges, warnings and forecasts"
  ],
